 "errors": [{"description": "Typo in the Type B case: ℓ is written as m+n instead of mn. The surrounding text immediately uses the correct value (1, mn) and the bound mn ≥ 4 holds, so the argument is unaffected.", "quote": "Then $\\ell = m+n \\ge 2\\cdot 2 = 4 > 1$, so the pair $(m,n)$ is replaced by $(1, mn)$"}],
 "notes": "Termination via product P (halves on g≥2) and count of 1's (strictly increases on g=1, never decreases) is rigorous. Existence of a surviving entry >1 is proved. Invariance of gcd of p-adic valuations under (α,β)→(min,|α−β|) is correctly shown, including the all-zero case, and yields M explicitly. Complete."}
